// A4 fuzz DIVERGE hunt (2026-09-07), root cause 1: `x op= e` used to push a
// lazy SYM(x) tag before compiling e -- a nested `let _ = x = .. in ..`
// inside e (reassigning x mid-expression) corrupted the combine step, which
// read x's NEW value instead of the value x held when the statement began.
// `x op= e` must snapshot x BEFORE e's side effects (x = x_old + e).
// EXPECT 103 from: hand: self-assignment
fn main() -> i64 { let v0 = 100; v0 += (let _ = v0 = 7 in 3); v0 }
